        "value": "<p><strong>IHC No. -&nbsp;514/2024</strong><br><strong>Gross :-&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>Received one paraffin tissue block no. <strong>24-3400</strong><br><strong>Clinical Details : Spindle cell lesion</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY RESULTS</strong></p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>IHC MARKER(S)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; RESULT</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CD117</td>\n<td>Non-Immunoreactive, score 0 in the lesional cells</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>DOG-1</td>\n<td>Non-Immunoreactive, score 0 in the lesional cells</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CD 34</td>\n<td>Non-Immunoreactive, score 0 in the lesional cells</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SMA</td>\n<td>Immunoreactive, score 3+ in the lesional cells</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>S-100</td>\n<td>Non-immunoreactive, score 0 in the lesional cells</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Comments : Advised clinico-radiological correlation</strong></p>\n<p><br><br><strong>INTERPRETATION</strong></p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;RESULT</strong></td>\n<td><strong>&nbsp; SCORE&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Non immunoreactive</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Immunoreactive in 1-25 % cells</td>\n<td>1+</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Immunoreactive in 26-50% cells</td>\n<td>2+</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Immunoreactive in 51-75% cells</td>\n<td>3+</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Immunoreactive in 76-100% cells&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</td>\n<td>4+</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><br>&nbsp;<strong>Notes :</strong></p>\n<p><br>&nbsp;1.&nbsp;This test was performed on paraffin embedded tissue section.<br>2.&nbsp;Detection system used &ndash; Biogenex &nbsp;Real Envision Detection system, peroxidase/ DAB + Rabbit/mouse.<br>3.&nbsp;The impression is based on the material submitted and is not a complete surgical pathlogy report.<br>4.&nbsp;Improper Fixation may affect results.&nbsp;<br>5.&nbsp;This assay has not been validated on decalified tissue. Results should be interpreted with caution given the likelihood or false negativity of decalcified specimen.</p>\n<p><br>&nbsp;<strong>Fixative requirement :</strong></p>\n<p><br>&nbsp;1.&nbsp;The volume of formalin fixative should be atleast 10 times the volume of the specimen<br>2.&nbsp;Specimens should be immersed in 10% neutral buffered formalin within 1 hours of the biopsy/ resection procedure ( time of removal&nbsp;and time of immersion to be mentioned )<br>3. In all resection (large) specimens , the tumour must be bisected prior to immersion in fixative.</p>",
